# Root .dockerignore — applies ONLY to builds whose context is the repo root,
# i.e. the production frontend image (Dockerfile.prod). The backend and dev
# frontend images build from their own directories and use their own
# .dockerignore files, so this file never affects them.
#
# Never ship host node_modules (Windows/macOS binaries would break the
# Linux-native install in the image), build output, or env files with secrets.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.local
*.log
.git
